WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.239 --> 00:00:05.078
- Hello Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael,

00:00:05.078 --> 00:00:06.589
my one word is Believe,

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:08.345
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:08.345 --> 00:00:10.439
all the major problems of the world.

00:00:10.439 --> 00:00:11.708
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:14.879
today I'm going to talk about
the seven fundamental truths

00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:16.656
that will change your life.

00:00:16.656 --> 00:00:18.183
And as always guys, as you're listening,

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:20.477
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:20.477 --> 00:00:21.799
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:24.694
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired,

00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:26.765
and the more you write
it down for yourself,

00:00:26.765 --> 00:00:29.575
the more likely it's going
to stick in here as well.

00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:30.408
Enjoy.

00:00:33.848 --> 00:00:36.431
(techno music)

00:00:41.935 --> 00:00:44.984
Truth number one is, You Are
What You Consistently Do.

00:00:44.984 --> 00:00:46.537
If you look at your calendar,
you look at what you're doing

00:00:46.537 --> 00:00:48.833
on a daily, regular basis,

00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:51.343
that is what's going to
determine your future path.

00:00:51.343 --> 00:00:53.592
So if you eat one chocolate bar,

00:00:53.592 --> 00:00:55.710
but the rest of your
day is pretty healthy,

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.081
you're going to be a healthy person.

00:00:57.081 --> 00:00:59.057
But if you're eating junk, and more junk,

00:00:59.057 --> 00:01:01.142
and then pizza, and then
Burger King, and more burgers,

00:01:01.142 --> 00:01:02.210
and more junk afterwards,

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.930
and then you eat one piece of broccoli,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.345
doesn't mean you're going to be healthy.

00:01:05.345 --> 00:01:08.058
Working out once won't make
a big difference for you.

00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:10.904
Working out three times a
week, or working out every day,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.306
you'll see changes in your life.

00:01:12.306 --> 00:01:13.987
And so if you apply that to your business,

00:01:13.987 --> 00:01:15.520
if you have a goal, if you have a dream,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.857
if you have something
and you want to pursue,

00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:19.866
you are what you consistently do.

00:01:19.866 --> 00:01:21.938
Doing it once is not enough.

00:01:21.938 --> 00:01:24.299
Doing it once a week is
likely not enough as well.

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:26.820
If you have a plan, you want
to accomplish a big goal,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.824
you need to find time every
single day to focus on it,

00:01:29.824 --> 00:01:32.552
to take some kind of movement
so you build a momentum,

00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:34.035
so that that dream happens.

00:01:34.035 --> 00:01:36.754
You are what you consistently do,

00:01:36.754 --> 00:01:39.171
not what's in the exceptions.

00:01:42.132 --> 00:01:45.085
Number two is, Your Daily
Habits Set You Up For Success.

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:48.093
So in order to be what
we consistently are,

00:01:48.093 --> 00:01:49.581
then you need to set up your day

00:01:49.581 --> 00:01:52.204
so that every morning
you create the routine

00:01:52.204 --> 00:01:53.835
that sets you up for that perfect day.

00:01:53.835 --> 00:01:57.100
I'm a big believer that
the first habit that you do

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.603
sets you up for the rest of the day.

00:01:58.603 --> 00:02:00.636
And so if you are
consistent with that habit,

00:02:00.636 --> 00:02:02.164
then you're consistent
with everything else

00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:04.707
that you want to do, so an
easy one is making the bed.

00:02:04.707 --> 00:02:06.244
So if you make the bed,

00:02:06.244 --> 00:02:08.132
then you're not just making the bed,

00:02:08.132 --> 00:02:10.571
you're the kind of person who sets a goal,

00:02:10.571 --> 00:02:11.779
and follows through.

00:02:11.779 --> 00:02:13.347
And then you're much more
likely to do the next step,

00:02:13.347 --> 00:02:14.668
and the next step, and the next step.

00:02:14.668 --> 00:02:16.395
So a lot of people have a daily routine.

00:02:16.395 --> 00:02:18.802
In an ideal world of,
I'm going to wake up,

00:02:18.802 --> 00:02:19.787
and I want to make the bed,

00:02:19.787 --> 00:02:21.604
and I want to have green tea,

00:02:21.604 --> 00:02:23.978
and I want to meditate, and I
want to do some yoga after that,

00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:26.090
and I want mindfulness, and gratefulness,

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:27.964
and I want to work out, and
then I'm going to start my day.

00:02:27.964 --> 00:02:29.691
You know, you have this huge long thing,

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:31.396
which is possible to do.

00:02:31.396 --> 00:02:33.604
But if your first thing is really hard,

00:02:33.604 --> 00:02:34.651
if you're goal for example,

00:02:34.651 --> 00:02:37.491
is I want to wake up, and I
want to go for a 30-minute run.

00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:38.715
That run is painful.

00:02:38.715 --> 00:02:39.698
Once you're running you're good,

00:02:39.698 --> 00:02:44.146
but getting the shoes on and
going out the door is painful.

00:02:44.146 --> 00:02:46.801
So it's much easier to
start with something simple.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.611
Because if likely, if you miss that run,

00:02:48.611 --> 00:02:49.972
you're going to miss everything else

00:02:49.972 --> 00:02:51.363
that's part of your schedule.

00:02:51.363 --> 00:02:53.404
But if you hit that run, you're
going to stay consistent.

00:02:53.404 --> 00:02:56.146
So that morning thing, the
very first thing that you do

00:02:56.146 --> 00:02:57.458
becomes super important.

00:02:57.458 --> 00:03:01.156
It's why I created the
Hashtag BTA for you guys.

00:03:01.156 --> 00:03:03.078
And what I wanted you to
do was wake up every day,

00:03:03.078 --> 00:03:04.977
watch a video that inspires you

00:03:04.977 --> 00:03:06.047
where you're learning something,

00:03:06.047 --> 00:03:07.943
and then write Hashtag BTA,

00:03:07.943 --> 00:03:11.160
with the number of consecutive
days you've left a comment,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.953
to keep the streak going.

00:03:12.953 --> 00:03:15.859
And it's not just giving you
the information in that video,

00:03:15.859 --> 00:03:19.078
but you're the kind of person
now who follows through.

00:03:19.078 --> 00:03:20.399
And if you start with that video,

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.813
you're much more likely
to do the next thing,

00:03:21.813 --> 00:03:23.622
and the next thing, and the next thing.

00:03:23.622 --> 00:03:25.701
And so create a daily
routine that supports you,

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:26.995
and sets you up for success,

00:03:26.995 --> 00:03:30.095
and make the first thing super easy to do,

00:03:30.095 --> 00:03:31.783
so that you're going to follow through,

00:03:31.783 --> 00:03:33.783
and keep the next one going,
and the next one going,

00:03:33.783 --> 00:03:35.700
and the next one going.

00:03:38.321 --> 00:03:39.914
Number three is, Your Environment Matters

00:03:39.914 --> 00:03:41.315
More Than You Think.

00:03:41.315 --> 00:03:43.170
This is the reason why people say you are

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.809
the result of the five people
closest to you in your life.

00:03:45.809 --> 00:03:47.665
Your environment really,
really, really matters,

00:03:47.665 --> 00:03:49.943
and most people have big goals of what

00:03:49.943 --> 00:03:51.540
they want to accomplish,

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.954
but they don't have the current
environment around them,

00:03:53.954 --> 00:03:56.764
that helps support them
achieving that big goal.

00:03:56.764 --> 00:03:58.244
And so look at your
friends, look at the people

00:03:58.244 --> 00:03:59.407
who you hang out with.

00:03:59.407 --> 00:04:01.381
Look at the magazines you're reading,

00:04:01.381 --> 00:04:03.310
and the videos you're watching.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:07.868
Do they consistently help
you become that person

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.060
that you want to become?

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.757
Are your friends pushing
you and guiding you,

00:04:10.757 --> 00:04:12.285
and motivating you, and supporting you?

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.588
Or are they telling
you, "You can't do that,

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:15.540
"you're never going to make it,

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.540
"you're not going to have success,

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.693
"who do you think you are to go off

00:04:17.693 --> 00:04:19.682
"and do that big scary thing?"

00:04:19.682 --> 00:04:20.634
And so your environment matters,

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.330
because if you're hanging
around these people

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.115
who are just putting you down,

00:04:24.115 --> 00:04:24.995
then what are you going to do?

00:04:24.995 --> 00:04:27.090
You're going to have moments of boldness,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.826
and then you're going to shrink back down.

00:04:28.826 --> 00:04:30.048
Because you want to be here,

00:04:30.048 --> 00:04:32.418
but your environment's keeping you here.

00:04:32.418 --> 00:04:34.338
And so whether it's
joining the meetup group,

00:04:34.338 --> 00:04:36.089
or watching YouTube videos,

00:04:36.089 --> 00:04:37.866
or looking at your physical environment,

00:04:37.866 --> 00:04:39.072
and what's on the walls,

00:04:39.072 --> 00:04:41.730
what's on the background of
your phone and your computer,

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:45.266
you want to be around the
things that make you come alive,

00:04:45.266 --> 00:04:48.676
and force you to think
big and bold consistently.

00:04:48.676 --> 00:04:50.602
It's why I helped create
this YouTube channel,

00:04:50.602 --> 00:04:52.362
it wasn't just for you guys, it's for me.

00:04:52.362 --> 00:04:54.714
Because I want to be
around successful people,

00:04:54.714 --> 00:04:56.900
doing big, bold, scary things,

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.602
so that I don't wake up and
just be comfortable every day.

00:04:59.602 --> 00:05:00.931
So I'm still pushing myself to get up

00:05:00.931 --> 00:05:05.014
and do bigger and bolder
things every single day.

00:05:07.182 --> 00:05:08.722
The fourth truth is,

00:05:08.722 --> 00:05:10.580
You Don't Need Anyone's Permission.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.296
So, from my personal experience,

00:05:12.296 --> 00:05:15.173
when I had to make a variety
of career changes in my life,

00:05:15.173 --> 00:05:17.874
going from a police officer in training,

00:05:17.874 --> 00:05:20.658
to going into sales, to thinking of being

00:05:20.658 --> 00:05:22.057
a marriage counselor.

00:05:22.057 --> 00:05:23.642
In all these things,

00:05:23.642 --> 00:05:26.194
I needed to make sure
that I do right by me.

00:05:26.194 --> 00:05:27.858
And so when I think of the life decisions

00:05:27.858 --> 00:05:29.363
that I have made in my life,

00:05:29.363 --> 00:05:31.684
I think of myself in
like in 40 or 50 years.

00:05:31.684 --> 00:05:33.996
Let's say I'm lying on my death bed.

00:05:33.996 --> 00:05:37.236
What kind of regrets
do I not want to have?

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.277
So I read an interesting blog
post by an Australian nurse,

00:05:40.277 --> 00:05:41.906
who takes care of dying people.

00:05:41.906 --> 00:05:44.636
She mentioned five things
that were in common

00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.579
with a huge number people,

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:47.724
and what they worried about,

00:05:47.724 --> 00:05:50.197
what kind of fears they had,
the kind of things they said.

00:05:50.197 --> 00:05:53.332
Interestingly enough, three
that really stood out for me,

00:05:53.332 --> 00:05:57.499
one, a lot of them said, "I
wish I let myself be happier."

00:05:59.023 --> 00:06:01.768
Second point is, I wish I had the courage

00:06:01.768 --> 00:06:04.098
to express my true feelings.

00:06:04.098 --> 00:06:06.454
And the third one was,
I wish I had the courage

00:06:06.454 --> 00:06:08.932
to live life to my true self,

00:06:08.932 --> 00:06:11.849
and not live to someone
else's expectations.

00:06:11.849 --> 00:06:14.117
So when you think of your life right now,

00:06:14.117 --> 00:06:16.265
and if you imagine in 40 years,

00:06:16.265 --> 00:06:18.456
maybe you want to try a new job,

00:06:18.456 --> 00:06:20.400
maybe you want to do a dance class,

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.042
maybe you want to ask someone out.

00:06:23.042 --> 00:06:24.715
Are you waiting for permission,

00:06:24.715 --> 00:06:27.667
and the funny thing is sometimes
it's not from other people.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.980
Sometimes it's just from yourself.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.725
Sometimes you're getting in your own way,

00:06:31.725 --> 00:06:33.021
because of fear of failure,

00:06:33.021 --> 00:06:35.124
because of fear of rejection,

00:06:35.124 --> 00:06:36.773
a variety of things.

00:06:36.773 --> 00:06:38.141
I'm going to tell you right now,

00:06:38.141 --> 00:06:39.964
it is an incredible feeling

00:06:39.964 --> 00:06:41.559
when you let that go,

00:06:41.559 --> 00:06:44.118
and you feel that you
deserve all the happiness

00:06:44.118 --> 00:06:46.790
that's out there waiting for you.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.525
Just make sure you consider it.

00:06:48.525 --> 00:06:50.491
Next time you get excited about something,

00:06:50.491 --> 00:06:52.765
next time you feel
passionate about something,

00:06:52.765 --> 00:06:54.422
next time you feel a little bit scared,

00:06:54.422 --> 00:06:56.081
but you want to try something,

00:06:56.081 --> 00:06:57.344
just do it.

00:06:57.344 --> 00:06:58.623
Don't get in your way,

00:06:58.623 --> 00:07:00.240
don't let others get in the way.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:02.302
You don't need other people's permission.

00:07:02.302 --> 00:07:04.492
At the end of the day,
30-40 years from now,

00:07:04.492 --> 00:07:07.377
I want you to make sure that
you're not living with regrets.

00:07:07.377 --> 00:07:09.460
So be free, and be happy.

00:07:13.038 --> 00:07:14.792
Truth number five is, Modeling Success

00:07:14.792 --> 00:07:16.241
Will Shortcut Your Path.

00:07:16.241 --> 00:07:17.423
Whatever you're trying to figure out,

00:07:17.423 --> 00:07:18.257
whatever goal you have,

00:07:18.257 --> 00:07:20.463
whatever ambition that you
want to go out and create,

00:07:20.463 --> 00:07:21.575
somebody has already done it.

00:07:21.575 --> 00:07:23.720
If they haven't done it exactly,

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.095
they've done it pretty closely.

00:07:25.095 --> 00:07:27.431
And so the more that you
can look to their story

00:07:27.431 --> 00:07:29.478
of how they went from startup to hitting

00:07:29.478 --> 00:07:31.084
that first big objectives,

00:07:31.084 --> 00:07:32.328
you can learn from that story,

00:07:32.328 --> 00:07:33.549
and apply it to yourself.

00:07:33.549 --> 00:07:35.740
If you look at Starbucks as an example.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:38.588
Howard Schultz, the
founder, went to Italy,

00:07:38.588 --> 00:07:40.789
and he was on vacation with his family,

00:07:40.789 --> 00:07:43.132
and he saw how the coffee shop was

00:07:43.132 --> 00:07:45.078
the center of life for Italians,

00:07:45.078 --> 00:07:46.406
it was their third home.

00:07:46.406 --> 00:07:47.902
They had home, they had work,

00:07:47.902 --> 00:07:49.580
and then they had the coffee shop.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.445
And the cafe was a sacred place

00:07:51.445 --> 00:07:53.716
that people liked to
hang out and belong to.

00:07:53.716 --> 00:07:55.236
He looked at the North American market,

00:07:55.236 --> 00:07:57.299
and he saw the Dunkin Donuts of the world,

00:07:57.299 --> 00:07:58.507
where it was just fast through,

00:07:58.507 --> 00:08:00.036
you go in, you come out.

00:08:00.036 --> 00:08:00.995
You know, you just get your coffee,

00:08:00.995 --> 00:08:02.460
you get your caffeine, and you leave.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:04.339
But it wasn't seen as that third home.

00:08:04.339 --> 00:08:06.858
And so he thought, "Why don't
I just bring this concept

00:08:06.858 --> 00:08:08.098
"to North America?"

00:08:08.098 --> 00:08:11.378
This concept that had worked
for decades for Italians,

00:08:11.378 --> 00:08:12.945
and just bring it to North America?

00:08:12.945 --> 00:08:15.387
And that's how Starbucks
was eventually born.

00:08:15.387 --> 00:08:16.634
And you can think of it as,

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:17.827
that's a meeting place for people,

00:08:17.827 --> 00:08:19.588
that's where people like
to spend their time,

00:08:19.588 --> 00:08:21.176
between home and work,

00:08:21.176 --> 00:08:22.987
and so that model really worked for him.

00:08:22.987 --> 00:08:24.571
Whatever goal you have,

00:08:24.571 --> 00:08:26.257
somebody has already figured it out,

00:08:26.257 --> 00:08:28.604
and by watching videos, or
by reading their stories,

00:08:28.604 --> 00:08:29.801
or listening to interviews,

00:08:29.801 --> 00:08:32.259
you can dissect it, and apply their rules

00:08:32.259 --> 00:08:35.342
to help you accomplish the same goal.

00:08:37.619 --> 00:08:39.675
Truth number six is,
Your Profits Will Come

00:08:39.675 --> 00:08:41.111
From Your Passion.

00:08:41.111 --> 00:08:43.867
If you look at anybody who's
had success in any field,

00:08:43.867 --> 00:08:47.797
it's because they had massive
love for what they're doing.

00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:49.807
You have to enjoy the work.

00:08:49.807 --> 00:08:52.951
Jerry Seinfeld calls it the
torture that you can endure.

00:08:52.951 --> 00:08:54.235
The things that you do,

00:08:54.235 --> 00:08:56.023
that you could do day in and day out,

00:08:56.023 --> 00:08:57.495
that you love so much that other people

00:08:57.495 --> 00:08:58.863
look at your schedule and say,

00:08:58.863 --> 00:09:00.711
"That is torture, that is crazy,

00:09:00.711 --> 00:09:02.766
"I can't believe how much
time you spend on it."

00:09:02.766 --> 00:09:06.031
People look at me filming
60 videos today and say,

00:09:06.031 --> 00:09:08.029
"That's nuts, how do you
do that all in one day,

00:09:08.029 --> 00:09:10.626
"it's crazy, I can barely
get one video up per week."

00:09:10.626 --> 00:09:14.195
It's torture to them, but to
me, I love it, I breath it.

00:09:14.195 --> 00:09:16.708
Helping entrepreneurs,
I can stay up all day,

00:09:16.708 --> 00:09:18.483
and not go to the bathroom, and not eat,

00:09:18.483 --> 00:09:19.403
and forget to sleep,

00:09:19.403 --> 00:09:21.147
just because I love helping entrepreneurs,

00:09:21.147 --> 00:09:22.764
and get so focused in that zone.

00:09:22.764 --> 00:09:23.938
Where other people would look at that

00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:24.802
and say it's torture.

00:09:24.802 --> 00:09:26.066
That's what you need to find.

00:09:26.066 --> 00:09:28.626
When you find that thing
that you love doing so much,

00:09:28.626 --> 00:09:31.549
and find a way to be able to
apply it to help other people,

00:09:31.549 --> 00:09:33.095
that's when you start making money.

00:09:33.095 --> 00:09:37.262
Your money, your profits will
come by pursuing your passion.

00:09:39.538 --> 00:09:43.132
Truth number seven is, You
Can Do What You Believe.

00:09:43.132 --> 00:09:44.384
Believe is a big thing for me,

00:09:44.384 --> 00:09:46.387
it's my one word, it's super important.

00:09:46.387 --> 00:09:49.963
But I find it so saddening to see people

00:09:49.963 --> 00:09:51.146
holding themselves back,

00:09:51.146 --> 00:09:53.042
not accomplishing the thing that I feel

00:09:53.042 --> 00:09:55.594
that they can do, that other
people think they can do,

00:09:55.594 --> 00:09:58.548
but they just don't have the
self confidence in themselves.

00:09:58.548 --> 00:10:00.419
There's an expression by
Henry Ford that saying,

00:10:00.419 --> 00:10:02.411
"Whether you believe that you can,

00:10:02.411 --> 00:10:05.451
"or you can't, you're right."

00:10:05.451 --> 00:10:09.259
If you think that being 65 is too old

00:10:09.259 --> 00:10:12.113
to start a company, your right.

00:10:12.113 --> 00:10:15.106
But Colonel Sanders did
it, and tons of success.

00:10:15.106 --> 00:10:18.410
If you believe that being 19 is too young

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.786
to start a company, you're right.

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:23.345
But lots of people have
come before you and done it.

00:10:23.345 --> 00:10:25.970
There are people who
have way fewer resources

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:28.010
than what you currently have right now.

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:29.546
Whatever reason you're
giving yourself right now

00:10:29.546 --> 00:10:31.338
for not being a success,

00:10:31.338 --> 00:10:33.618
whether you're blaming your
government, or your country,

00:10:33.618 --> 00:10:36.203
or your gender, or your size, or your age,

00:10:36.203 --> 00:10:37.666
or your education, or your family,

00:10:37.666 --> 00:10:38.833
whatever it is that you're blaming,

00:10:38.833 --> 00:10:39.666
whatever the reason is,

00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:42.106
that you think you can't be successful,

00:10:42.106 --> 00:10:45.415
there are already people
who look exactly like you,

00:10:45.415 --> 00:10:47.124
who come from worse backgrounds,

00:10:47.124 --> 00:10:50.052
had less resources than you
currently have right now,

00:10:50.052 --> 00:10:51.249
and they've gone off and achieved

00:10:51.249 --> 00:10:53.674
much bigger things than you have.

00:10:53.674 --> 00:10:55.827
If they can do it, you can too,

00:10:55.827 --> 00:10:57.182
you just have to believe.

00:10:57.182 --> 00:10:59.369
So that's my take on the
seven fundamental truths

00:10:59.369 --> 00:11:00.442
that will change your life.

00:11:00.442 --> 00:11:02.507
I'd love to know, what did you guys think,

00:11:02.507 --> 00:11:04.005
which one was your favorite and why?

00:11:04.005 --> 00:11:06.182
What are you going to
immediately apply somehow

00:11:06.182 --> 00:11:07.708
to your life, or your business?

00:11:07.708 --> 00:11:08.925
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:11:08.925 --> 00:11:10.414
I'm super curious to find out.

00:11:10.414 --> 00:11:12.329
Also, did I miss an eight, nine, 10,

00:11:12.329 --> 00:11:13.789
that you want to add to the list?

00:11:13.789 --> 00:11:15.224
Let me know by leaving a comment.

00:11:15.224 --> 00:11:16.359
I also want to give a quick shout

00:11:16.359 --> 00:11:17.631
to Anthony Avina.

00:11:17.631 --> 00:11:19.093
Anthony thank you so much for picking up

00:11:19.093 --> 00:11:21.172
a copy of my book, Your One Word,

00:11:21.172 --> 00:11:23.217
and doing that review on your blog.

00:11:23.217 --> 00:11:24.604
I really, really appreciate it man,

00:11:24.604 --> 00:11:26.164
and I'm glad you enjoyed the book.

00:11:26.164 --> 00:11:27.414
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:11:27.414 --> 00:11:28.575
I believe in you.

00:11:28.575 --> 00:11:30.488
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:11:30.488 --> 00:11:32.622
and whatever your one word is.

00:11:32.622 --> 00:11:33.806
Much love.

00:11:33.806 --> 00:11:35.389
I'll see you soon.

